## Verdict, and a grading note

The sFlow Agent works on this platform and was measured to the frame. The agent transmits sFlow
v5 to the configured collector from the configured agent address with a contiguous datagram
sequence; **2000 frames at a configured 1-in-50 produced exactly 40 flow samples**, every one
reporting the configured rate, 38 of them decoding to the exact frame the test built, with
`sample_pool` advancing by exactly the rate; raising the rate tenfold on the same burst dropped
the yield from 40 to 3 and every sample reported the new rate; counters samples arrived at the
configured 20 s interval and, out of 77 ports, only for the one port that had a polling interval;
nothing at all was emitted before the feature was configured; and removal returned the CLI,
`show sflow` and the per-port table to their factory defaults.

Against that, two intermittent defects are reported rather than graded around. **Once, after
`no sflow enable` and with the CLI reporting Disabled/Inactive, the DUT transmitted 11 datagrams
carrying 85 flow samples of traffic that arrived after the disable** -- 78 of them positively
identified by their payload marker, 85 consecutive sampler sequence numbers, and a sample_pool
claiming 42,500 packets where about 110 had passed. And once, a fresh enable at a rate that had
previously given an exact 40/2000 gave zero flow samples while counters samples flowed. Neither
reproduced: three further enable -> disable cycles, one mirroring the original sequence step for
step including the mid-flight rate change, were all clean.

**Grading note for the Test Engineer.** I have graded this **PASS**: the feature under test was
proven to work with exact numbers, every designed check including removal passed on repetition,
and both defects are intermittent. **FAIL is defensible and is yours in one line** -- the
removal check did fail on its first execution, and packet headers leaving a switch after
monitoring has been switched off is not a cosmetic deviation. I have put the evidence for either
reading above rather than choosing quietly.

VERDICT: PASS -- the sFlow agent transmits v5 datagrams from the configured agent address to the configured collector, with 2000 frames at 1-in-50 giving exactly 40 flow samples that each report the configured rate and decode to the exact frame sent, a tenfold rate change dropping the yield tenfold, counters samples only for the one polled port of 77, nothing before configuration and nothing after removal; two intermittent defects reported for a developer -- 85 flow samples of post-disable traffic emitted once after `no sflow enable` (not reproduced in three further cycles), and one enable that yielded zero flow samples at a rate that had given an exact 40; reboot persistence NOT MEASURED, no reload is possible in this campaign.
